# Cargo.lock is committed (not gitignored): this workspace will grow a CLI
# binary crate in a later phase, and cargo's own guidance is to check in the
# lockfile for binaries. It also pins `zeroize` to 1.7.0 -- see
# docs/crypto-core.md -- which an uncommitted lockfile would let `cargo
# update` silently undo.

